%description:
Round-trip serialization test for the packet serializers: the captures that do NOT
round-trip yet.

Same engine as serializer_pcap -- deserialize each record of a pcap file into typed
chunks with the generic PacketDissector, re-serialize, compare byte-by-byte -- but
over the captures whose frames INET cannot reproduce today. Each one is a
documented model or serializer gap; the cause, the fix and the size of that fix are
in tests/unit/SERIALIZER_REMAINING_GAPS.md.

The counts below are pinned, so this test fails in BOTH directions: when a gap gets
worse or spreads, and when one is fixed. The latter is intentional -- a fixed
capture belongs in serializer_pcap, which guards it from then on, and the pinned
counts here plus SERIALIZER_REMAINING_GAPS.md have to follow. A partially fixed
capture stays here with lower numbers.

Adding a capture that does not round-trip means one line below (with the gap named
in a comment), the updated counts, and a row in SERIALIZER_REMAINING_GAPS.md.

Four of these captures fail on a few frames only. Their round-tripping frames are cut
out into pcap/derived/ and replayed by serializer_pcap as well, so the serializers
behind them do get a byte-exactness gate; see pcap/derived/README.md.

The coverage report is printed here as well, but it covers these captures only; the
serializer inventory ("USED ..." / "UNTESTED ...") is the one in serializer_pcap.

%includes:
#include "SerializerTestLib.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;

%activity:

// keep the output quiet: per-frame progress is logged at EV_TRACE (drop the log
// level to see it when debugging a hard crash); results are logged at EV_WARN
cLog::logLevel = LOGLEVEL_WARN;

beginSerializerCoverage();

// 9 frames differ: the on-wire order of the INIT/INIT-ACK parameters is not
// preserved (the model has fixed fields instead of an ordered parameter list)
testPcapSerialization("../../pcap/wireshark/sctp-www.cap", false);

// 9 frames differ: the mobility options trailing a Binding Update / Acknowledgement
// are not modelled
testPcapSerialization("../../pcap/mipv6.pcap", false);

// 4 frames differ: DhcpOptions is a fixed struct, not the option TLV list of the RFC
testPcapSerialization("../../pcap/dhcp.pcap", false);

// 802.11 control frames of subtypes INET does not model, so the MAC header
// deserializer marks the chunk incorrect: 8 VHT/HE NDP Announcements here and
// 1 Trigger frame in the aggregation capture. Both are radiotap/plain 802.11
// captures whose FCS presence the PcapReader detects per frame.
testPcapSerialization("../../pcap/wlan-blockack-reassoc.pcap", false);
testPcapSerialization("../../pcap/wlan-aggregation.pcap", false);

// 6 frames error: an ESP packet cannot be round-tripped from a capture at all --
// its trailer sits inside the encrypted region
testPcapSerialization("../../pcap/esp.pcap", false);


reportSerializerCoverage();

%contains: stdout
Files:  6 tested, 0 clean, 6 with differences

%contains: stdout
Frames: 341 total, 304 same, 22 differ, 15 error, 0 truncated

%not-contains: stdout
TOPLEVEL-RAWBYTES
